msgstr "This verb gates nothing today. /api/llm.chat is the only LLM endpoint and it answers to LLM write, so there is nothing left for read to govern. The switch is granted and locked rather than denied, because storing it as \"off\" would be permanent: filling in a missing permission only ever adds what a grant lacks, so nothing would widen it if a later release gives this verb something real to gate."

