msgid "This verb gates nothing today. Every message history call the API offers is a read, and rows are written by the sending pipeline itself, never by anything you can call. The switch is granted and locked rather than denied, because storing it as \"off\" would be permanent: filling in a missing permission only ever adds what a grant lacks, so nothing would widen it if a later release gives this verb something real to gate."
msgstr "This verb gates nothing today. Every message history call the API offers is a read, and rows are written by the sending pipeline itself, never by anything you can call. The switch is granted and locked rather than denied, because storing it as \"off\" would be permanent: filling in a missing permission only ever adds what a grant lacks, so nothing would widen it if a later release gives this verb something real to gate."

#: src/services/api/permissions.ts:864
msgid "This verb gates nothing today. Exactly one inbound webhook event call is permission-checked and it is a read; the rows themselves arrive on the provider callback routes /webhooks/email and /webhooks/email/inbound, which carry no workspace session and so consult no grant. Unlike the two verbs the matrix locks on, this one is still yours to switch — turning it off simply changes nothing today."
msgstr "This verb gates nothing today. Exactly one inbound webhook event call is permission-checked and it is a read; the rows themselves arrive on the provider callback routes /webhooks/email and /webhooks/email/inbound, which carry no workspace session and so consult no grant. Unlike the two verbs the matrix locks on, this one is still yours to switch — turning it off simply changes nothing today."

